        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "0ad7a564-c29b-36ff-b781-ac1e8cb14ce1",
                "word": "synchroniquement",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5b14818c-158b-3ebd-9a28-249afda184bc",
                        "entry_id": "0ad7a564-c29b-36ff-b781-ac1e8cb14ce1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "D’une manière synchronique. Du point de vue synchronique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c00eca97-9523-4c8c-9932-10fdd4af1aea",
                                "sense_id": "5b14818c-158b-3ebd-9a28-249afda184bc",
                                "text": "On peut se demander si les deux timbales [chez la cigale] vibrent synchroniquement pendant le chant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8f72cfa-02e9-48b6-89d9-c4d488ae935d",
                                "sense_id": "5b14818c-158b-3ebd-9a28-249afda184bc",
                                "text": "Comme beaucoup de ceux qui ont vécu au contact de la douce foule végétale, je connais sa bienveillance, et je regimbe devant un rythme artificiel qui transforme la germination et la lente croissance en ruées, les éclosions en bâillements de fauves, le gloxinia en trappe, le lys en crocodile et les haricots en hydres. Si l’on me veut faire accepter la gigantisation du cinéma, qu’on m’y donne, synchroniquement et à mensonge égal, le vacarme de la plante, mille fois grossi lui aussi, le tonnerre des floraisons, la canonnades des cosses éclatés et la balistique des semences."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "481b19dd-56e9-4278-ae6d-8a932bafadbe",
                                "sense_id": "5b14818c-158b-3ebd-9a28-249afda184bc",
                                "text": "Une partition d’orchestre n’a de sens que lue diachroniquement selon un axe (page après page, de gauche à droite), mais en même temps, synchroniquement selon l’autre axe, de haut en bas."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c9538c73-b4ca-4685-924b-c671a6562ab9",
                        "source_entry_id": "0ad7a564-c29b-36ff-b781-ac1e8cb14ce1",
                        "source_sense_id": "5b14818c-158b-3ebd-9a28-249afda184bc",
                        "target_lang_word": "synchronically",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "synchronically",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cfd5a9a6-a00d-31bd-a279-84ae3bfdadd0",
                                        "entry_id": "ac747ba1-21c3-31fe-aebc-ddc500221962",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a synchronic way; at the same time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb447987-9399-4b7f-9bb5-77d2bfdf072c",
                                                "sense_id": "cfd5a9a6-a00d-31bd-a279-84ae3bfdadd0",
                                                "text": "In particular, risks can pile up not only synchronically, as in multi premise deductions, but also diachronically, when a subject extends her knowledge by competent deduction from just one premise."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6adf00e-3fc4-49b3-b863-4eb1d8974e48",
                                                "sense_id": "cfd5a9a6-a00d-31bd-a279-84ae3bfdadd0",
                                                "text": "A story, a science fiction film, or, in fact, a scientific theory, can thus be positioned at a higher and later turning of the spiral, diachronically, but synchronically it can be a performance of a pattern or theme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47842ac4-8280-4633-a6ca-e746415bb43b",
                                                "sense_id": "cfd5a9a6-a00d-31bd-a279-84ae3bfdadd0",
                                                "text": "He divides synchronically opaque Sardinian toponyms into segments supposedly related to Basque lexical roots. For instance, the Ogliastan toponyms Dolai, Dodoliai and Iridolai, analyzd as *dol-ai, *do-dol-iai and *iri-dol-ai, in his view, all three contain a cognate of Bq. odol 'blood'."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
